Replace the sealed-import incumbents REFUSAL with purge-and-fresh-sealed-
reimport.  The refusal guarded against foreign r7_encoder modules; purging
achieves the same isolation strictly better, and the import that follows
re-verifies every closure file hash on every construction.  Without this,
any second codec-adapter construction in one process (candidate factories,
post-preparation probes, MTP) dies.  malaiwah declared extension, disclosed.
--- a/src/quant_pipeline/codecs/exl3_mcg.py
+++ b/src/quant_pipeline/codecs/exl3_mcg.py
@@ -126,7 +126,8 @@
         root = str(self.source_root)
         incumbents = sorted(name for name in sys.modules if name == "r7_encoder" or name.startswith("r7_encoder."))
         if incumbents:
-            raise RuntimeError(f"refusing cached r7_encoder modules before sealed import: {incumbents}")
+            for name in incumbents:
+                sys.modules.pop(name, None)
         if root in sys.path:
             sys.path.remove(root)
         sys.path.insert(0, root)
